#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309030 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "064d3c62-5cfc-502b-aba4-48e40042593f" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula for Cosine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db6c166e-72c3-552d-b524-d11113f0a364" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi^2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309032} {:answer/id #uuid "76d59c68-af09-5e9e-a3c5-93ed10ab20f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi^2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309033}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db6c166e-72c3-552d-b524-d11113f0a364" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\pi^2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309032} :answer-field/id #uuid "98143ef5-3ba7-5bf3-8e38-a70e9df4babe" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309031}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3ea82d24-c80c-5089-8bd5-efac42e51f83" :question/math-academy-id "q-348724" :question/problem "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡3x-2{sin}^{2}⁡3x+6x)\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Here, we use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nLetting $\\theta =3x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x={cos}^{2}⁡3x-{sin}^{2}⁡3x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}(2{cos}^{2}⁡3x-2{sin}^{2}⁡3x+6x)\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡6x+6x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\frac{2}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+\\frac{6}{2}{x}^{2})|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡6x+3{x}^{2})|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\pi )+3{(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}^{2}]-[\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )+3{(\\frac{\\pi }{6})}^{2}] \\\\  & =3(\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}}{36}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2{\\pi }^{2}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186309062 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "064d3c62-5cfc-502b-aba4-48e40042593f" :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Expressions Using the Double-Angle Formula for Cosine"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b1df459-e9e7-5e24-ae93-8f0ff084df92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309064} {:answer/id #uuid "927025b0-c583-5026-b39b-a84e6e40b2d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+1+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309065} {:answer/id #uuid "718e047b-bdee-561c-a8c7-ab2fa2e7ff19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+1+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309066} {:answer/id #uuid "519c467f-ada4-539f-8dfb-7981817b82dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309067} {:answer/id #uuid "ac2ffba9-fc21-5cdd-a62e-13a587b0f243" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309068}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b1df459-e9e7-5e24-ae93-8f0ff084df92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+x+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309064} :answer-field/id #uuid "9503887d-706b-5511-bfd5-17f38263336e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309063}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "12b0a367-b2dc-50bf-a676-57aa1201b034" :question/math-academy-id "q-74403" :question/problem "$\\int (3{cos}^{2}⁡x+1-3{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x=$" :question/worked-solution "We can use the double-angle formula for cosine:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta -{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{cos}⁡2\\theta \n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (3{cos}^{2}⁡x+1-3{sin}^{2}⁡x)\\text{d}x & =\\int [3({cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x)+1]\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int (3\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3(\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)+x+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x+x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
